KS-1282 | GET /api/platform/tenants: the requireSuperAdmin guard (platform.ts:222) is pinned by no connector cell | state In Progress | archivedAt None | branchName feature/ks-1282-get-apiplatformtenants-the-requiresuperadmin-guard | attachments [('1096', 'contributes')] | comments 0
   --- DESCRIPTION KS-1282 ---
## BLUF

The `requireSuperAdmin` guard on `GET /api/platform/tenants` (api-gateway `routes/platform.ts:222`) is pinned by no connector cell. With that one line deleted, 0 of 646 api-gateway cells go red, and a connector key then lists tenants: 200, with `GET /api/tenants` called using the connector JWT (in-process probe). Surfaced by the #1084-#1091 gate.

## Recommendation

Add one connector cell that expects 403 FORBIDDEN on `GET /api/platform/tenants` and no upstream call, then measure the other `requireSuperAdmin` guards in platform.ts the same way. Not urgent: nothing here shows the guard is wrong today, only that no test would catch its removal.

## Detail

* **Measured by the batch gate** `2026-09-19-batch1084-1091-tier1-r1` **(row N91-2, tamper TENANTSGETUNGUARDED):** the `    requireSuperAdmin,` line of the 4-line block `  router.get(` / `    '/api/platform/tenants',` / `    authenticateToken(),` / `    requireSuperAdmin,` (block at :219, guard at :222) deleted: 0 of 641 red at #1091's head, 0 of 646 with all eight merged (develop `4273adfac`).
* The line text `    requireSuperAdmin,` occurs 13 times in platform.ts. :239 (`POST /api/platform/tenants`) is now pinned by #1091's cell. :222 is the one measured here. **The other 11 are unmeasured.** Any tamper on this text must be located by a scope anchor, never by the first occurrence: the first occurrence IS :222.
* It is an authorisation gap (who may list tenants), not a Bearer-forwarding one: the GET forwards the connector JWT, not the caller's Bearer. That is why it sits outside the connector-Bearer ticket it was found beside.
* Filed by Seat B 6th on 2026-09-19, as Wednesday ruled (one ticket, facts only).
   --- END ---
